{"title":"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If in applying the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_formula\" title=\"Quadratic formula\">quadratic formula</a> to a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_equation\" title=\"Quadratic equation\">quadratic equation</a>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/374d97e46af67598981023916cf227b57d977e17.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) \\equiv ax^2 + bx + c = 0,\\]\" width=\"194\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>it happens that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1638a5afe23e37a47b22120de3f000ab96d554bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{b^2}{4a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"39\" />, then the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b87bab82790e7da89285041886327223094f8171.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> will certainly:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/e/a6e389b134ee83ba9ddcf3f9714319fd7ec991d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ have\\ a\\ maximum  } \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ have\\ a\\ minimum} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"400\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd6fe5a8198b9747e7f97c5c8ea7c77b5ac1a32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(C) \\ be\\ tangent\\ to\\ the\\ x-axis} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a02a92b6131a62c42491688120e0274ea6960019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(D) \\ be\\ tangent\\ to\\ the\\ y-axis} \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"274\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f734a89653fe796de9cdfca7b2955d44613fad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(E) \\ lie\\ in\\ one\\ quadrant\\ only}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Discriminant\" title=\"Discriminant\">discriminant</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/2502434d8d3417bd8e4f9b3a535e72143a6853c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - 4ac = b^2 - 4a\\left(\\frac{b^2}{4a}\\right) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has exactly one root (with multiplicity 2). At this root, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> will therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/b/f0b5b8612c27666a237e62536f450101eed270dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{be tangent to the }x\\text{-axis}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"223\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>A is false as if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> will have a minimum, not a maximum.\n</p><p>B is false as if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> will have a maximum, not a minimum.\n</p><p>D is false as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is continuous for all real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so it will cross through the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis instead of being tangent.\n</p><p>E is false as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is defined for all real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so it must lie in at least two quadrants.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME\" title=\"1951 AHSME\">1951 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1951 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1951\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1951 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1951_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"19